WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.601 --> 00:00:02.868
-James, can I get some thank-you
note writing music, please?

00:00:02.868 --> 00:00:06.767
♪♪
[ Laughter ]

00:00:06.767 --> 00:00:09.133
-I guess he melted.
-It's beautiful.

00:00:11.701 --> 00:00:14.467
Thank you, this season of
"The Bachelorette,"

00:00:14.467 --> 00:00:17.567
for having two Bachelorettes,
which sounds crazy

00:00:17.567 --> 00:00:18.801
until you realize it also has

00:00:18.801 --> 00:00:21.667
two Justins, two Jareds,
and 38 Jordan R's.

00:00:21.667 --> 00:00:23.868
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:27.334
"I'm Jordan R.
I'm an entrepreneur."

00:00:30.767 --> 00:00:34.367
Thank you, "The Gray Man," for
being a new Netflix thriller

00:00:34.367 --> 00:00:37.000
about two men fighting to
the death over whether

00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:39.834
it's spelled
G-R-A-Y or G-R-E-Y.

00:00:39.834 --> 00:00:42.133
[ Laughter ]
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:42.133 --> 00:00:44.667
"Are you from England?"

00:00:44.667 --> 00:00:46.400
If you're from the U.K.

00:00:50.067 --> 00:00:54.133
Thank you, eating s'mores around
a campfire, for making sure

00:00:54.133 --> 00:00:56.267
I'm nowhere near a sink or
a napkin after holding

00:00:56.267 --> 00:00:57.968
the stickiest food ever made.

00:00:57.968 --> 00:01:01.334
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Rub dirt.

00:01:01.334 --> 00:01:03.734
-Rub dirt on it?
-I don't know.

00:01:06.801 --> 00:01:10.601
-Thank you, Delta Airlines
flight that blew out two tires

00:01:10.601 --> 00:01:13.868
while landing at LAX,
or as Spirit Airlines put,

00:01:13.868 --> 00:01:16.334
"See, that's what you get for
having planes with wheels."

00:01:16.334 --> 00:01:18.133
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:21.968 --> 00:01:23.801
Don't want to say I told you so.

00:01:26.200 --> 00:01:30.434
Thank you, air conditioners and
Hot Pockets, for being two ways

00:01:30.434 --> 00:01:32.100
to keep things cold
on the inside

00:01:32.100 --> 00:01:33.434
when it's hot on the outside.

00:01:33.434 --> 00:01:35.868
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:35.868 --> 00:01:38.400
Just keep eating it.
It'll cool off.

00:01:42.734 --> 00:01:46.033
Thank you, popsicles, for making
your 7-year-old look like

00:01:46.033 --> 00:01:47.801
they just took down
a bottle of Merlot.

00:01:47.801 --> 00:01:50.400
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:01:57.868 --> 00:01:59.767
Thank you, string cheese,

00:01:59.767 --> 00:02:02.133
for looking like mozzarella
sticks at a nude beach.

00:02:02.133 --> 00:02:04.634
There you have it, everybody.
Those are my thank-you notes.

